nodecode-fish-audio is a rewrite of 100yenadmin's 100yenadmin/fish-audio-hermes:

  https://github.com/100yenadmin/fish-audio-hermes
  commit 606afb54aa1a354cc8eac0b17f3da3a105ac55a7
  Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 Electric Sheep (100yenadmin) (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the three tools and their whole call path -- fish_speak's text,
voice, model, format, speed, language and multi-speaker arguments, the
bracket emotion cues passed through to the model that reads them, the
prosody/speed body and the model header, and the saved, never-overwritten
audio file the answer names; fish_transcribe's upload of a local file with
timestamps, diarization, speaker hints, audio-event tags and the SRT written
beside the audio; fish_voices' search, this-account listing, single voice
and clone-from-samples, including the speaker-consent gate and the private
or unlisted visibility a clone lands in; the per-profile section for the key
(an inline secret or the environment variable it names), the base URL, the
speech and transcription models, the default voice, the output container and
the folder the files go to; the refusals that cost nothing -- an empty text,
a speed out of range, an unreadable or oversize file, a kind Fish Audio does
not take, a missing key -- and Fish Audio's own sentence plus the fix for a
failed status; and the /fish command, which prints the settings, searches
the library and shows one voice.

Left out: the Hermes-only surfaces -- the registered TTS and STT providers
that make Fish speak every reply, the two hooks that append MEDIA tags and
ask before a clone, the Desktop app and its dashboard backend, and the CLI
setup wizard -- because a Nodecode cell contributes tools and a command, not
a harness provider, and none of the Desktop code runs outside Hermes. Also
left out: word-level timestamps on speech (Fish's SSE endpoint), custom
pronunciation dictionaries, voice design and the save-a-design receipt, and
saved voice-name aliases; each is another endpoint or another store, and the
tools here cover the same purpose without them. The plugin's plugin.yaml
settings schema became the cell's fish-audio config section.
